#ignores the target directory but from ur local machine. .gitignore does that, but since we are using docker,
# your device that will run the build will have its own target directory to copy, but u wanna be careful because
# it might break the docker build.

#Imagine the image docker uses is in Unix but yours is in windows. it will copy from windows to unix and it might
# break the build at the "COPY . ." command in the backend Dockerfile. So we ignore the target directory from our local
#machine, but the image will have its own target directory to copy.

target
.env
